  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Realizing Minimum Living Standards for Disadvantaged Communities through peace building and village-based economic development</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Between 1999 and 2002, Indonesia&apos;s Maluku islands were the scene of a violent conflict that claimed the lives of several thousand people and caused displacement of half a million. To tackle the challenge of improving the human security and enhance the social fabric of the conflict affected population, UNIDO and ILO joined forces and started a comprehensive intervention in 2009 financed through the United Nations Trust Fund for Human Security (UNTFHS).</narrative>
  </description>
